1. `Debug.Assert(New_Ret < 0 || arrList.Contains(x));`

This assert statement is added in the `PUT_IndexOfContract` method. The purpose is to verify that the return value of the `IndexOf` method is negative or the new list still contains the element `x`. This is important because if the `IndexOf` returns a negative value, it means that the element `x` is not in the list. Therefore, we need to verify that the new list still contains `x` when the return value is negative.

2. `Debug.Assert(New_Ret == -1 || arrList.Contains(x));`

This assert statement is added in the `PUT_LastIndexOfContract` method. The purpose is similar to the previous one. The `LastIndexOf` method returns the index of the last occurrence of an element in a list or -1 if the element is not found. Hence, we need to check if the new list still contains `x` when the return value is -1.
